# This file names what a change can do that no later check would catch, not
# where a file lives. GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so the order
# below is the whole mechanism: kept paths first, then lines that name no owner
# and so release documents and the like, then paths that must stay owned
# whatever came before, then the shared lines from templates/codeowners.
# Those shared lines stay last (SYNC-1): this repo's own lines go above them,
# never after. There is no catch-all line, by design.
#
# This repo does not require code-owner review (REPO-1), so these lines request
# a review and do not block a merge by themselves; the merge route reads them.
# tools/tests/codeowners_ownership.py checks a fixed table of sample paths
# against this file, and it runs in CI through `pnpm selftest`.

# Kept: the code of every gate other repos run, the floors and exemption
# definitions they read, and the tests of those gates (the rules themselves).
/tools/                              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# Kept: ruleset definitions, the CODEOWNERS template and the file that sets how
# it is compared, and the workflow template.
/templates/rulesets/                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/templates/org-rulesets/             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/templates/codeowners                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/templates/manifest.tsv              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/templates/workflows/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# Kept: the TS-4 floor tiers, which tools/check-tsconfig.sh reads directly.
/packages/tsconfig/*.json            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Released: documents, and discovery files that report and judge nothing. These
# name no owner and come after the kept directories above so they win.
/tools/**/*.md
/templates/**/*.md
/tools/clause-paths.tsv
/packages/tsconfig/package.json

# Kept again, after the releases above, so that no release line can ever
# un-own a floor or a mode definition: the thresholds, the promoted-gate
# register and the docs-site tiers.
/tools/thresholds.tsv                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/tools/ts-promoted.tsv               @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/tools/docs-site-tiers.tsv           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Kept at any depth: the rulebook, CODEOWNERS files, registry settings and the
# floor files other repos name. A document extension never releases these.
CLAUDE.md                            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
AUTHORISATIONS.md                    @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/CODEOWNERS                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/.npmrc                            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/floors.tsv                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# Kept: legal text.
/LICENSE                             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/LICENSE-DOCS                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Shared lines from templates/codeowners. They stay last (SYNC-1).
/.standardsignore        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards.mode         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.docs-lint*             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards-db-tooling   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
